        "id": 1000262
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-25T00:48:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@amaiorano@google.com `--disable-dawn-features\u003duse_dxc` affects the Dawn toggles, of which there is already one called \"UseDXC\". Since Chromium [returns a hardcoded value of \"true\"](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:gpu/command_buffer/service/dawn_platform.cc;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1;l\u003d241?q\u003dDawnPlatform::IsFeatureEnabled\u0026gsn\u003dIsFeatureEnabled\u0026gs\u003dKYTHE%3A%2F%2Fkythe%3A%2F%2Fchromium.googlesource.com%2Fcodesearch%2Fchromium%2Fsrc%2F%2Fmain%3Flang%3Dc%252B%252B%3Fpath%3Dgpu%2Fcommand_buffer%2Fservice%2Fdawn_platform.cc%23l9VrmsHBOCZhCYjGq7yyf31jOtxIXzSX4FdiZv1PeF4) for `kWebGPUUseDXC`, the DAWN_CHECK I added here does not fire when I pass this command line flag. \n\nThere is a existing crbug to [delete kWebGPUUseDXC](https://issues.chromium.org/issues/362247692). Happy to do remove the flag (but still keep the toggle) as a separate change if you\u0027d like. Are there people who set the feature flag to anything other than true? \n\nFor this CL, I\u0027ll set the toggle\u0027s default value to the value of the feature flag as Corentin suggests. I didn\u0027t realize `IsFeatureEnabled` can be overridden by the host.",
      "parentUuid": "c2f28b4e_ac554345",
      "revId": "f5c8223e93d3d1331a17bc53ec820fd523d03380",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
